tion/id #uuid "4fa12227-09f8-5d99-a2be-207b65a88fe1" :question/math-academy-id "q-319890" :question/problem "Calculate $AB+AC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & \\sqrt{3}-1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n|  |  | $0$ | $0$ | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $AB+AC=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $2$ |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | {{field-3}} | $0$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "We can apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nAB+AC=A(B+C).\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $B+C$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B+C & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 & \\sqrt{3}-1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & \\sqrt{3} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB+AC & =A(B+C) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & \\sqrt{3} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & \\sqrt{3} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299811 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115227 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8feeacff-b07d-5f98-a765-4d8571674a7a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Associative Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5380e4f7-3997-5eec-a4c1-2dd08757f0a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297904}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5380e4f7-3997-5eec-a4c1-2dd08757f0a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297904} :answer-field/id #uuid "2488bf7b-4c5f-5b36-8cbb-ca49d28d8bf9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298761} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07a31a1b-94aa-5cea-9846-cc139c0dc4ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "78" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07a31a1b-94aa-5cea-9846-cc139c0dc4ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "78" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297589} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ab1180c-fa05-5dcf-b73c-82d0a580b13c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299102} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27f662dc-9756-5093-86b7-94ddad217ede" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-182" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27f662dc-9756-5093-86b7-94ddad217ede" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-182" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297722} :answer-field/id #uuid "a09c47e6-4da3-5f54-947d-4183a7d968e3" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299170}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5aecc675-116f-5b56-855b-8a2ff5a85c00" :question/math-academy-id "q-319943" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $ABC=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix, $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix, and $C$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3\\times 2$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $1\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding only $1$ entry.\n\nSo, we find the product $BC$ first: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-20-6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-26\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $A$ by $BC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =A(BC) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-26\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}78 \\\\ -52 \\\\ -182\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485578 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115227 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8feeacff-b07d-5f98-a765-4d8571674a7a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Associative Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c8bceae-a8f8-59df-9913-53898f44b673" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485052}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c8bceae-a8f8-59df-9913-53898f44b673" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485052} :answer-field/id #uuid "16cf85a0-d4e0-503b-a40c-377068739a10" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485376} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df658338-ffbc-54a4-8fc3-4233fa4b9c9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df658338-ffbc-54a4-8fc3-4233fa4b9c9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485286} :answer-field/id #uuid "91a5a09a-06e9-5e46-b927-635849a5367f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485429} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3e847ec-d131-5985-94dc-25f91ed6df64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485336}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3e847ec-d131-5985-94dc-25f91ed6df64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485336} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc2e3df9-3029-583e-b5fd-63d9b4b790dc" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485478}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c4c5958e-629a-595b-ba26-53d736ebe0b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-320017" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $ABC=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, and $C$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix. Therefore,\n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$ gives a $3\\times 3$ matrix, which would require finding $9$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$ gives a $2\\times 1$ matrix, which requires finding $2$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $BC$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $A$ by $BC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =A(BC) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -15 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299814 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115227 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8feeacff-b07d-5f98-a765-4d8571674a7a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Associative Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6482cff8-ea84-5d14-a24d-9034a0c7b0a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297981}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6482cff8-ea84-5d14-a24d-9034a0c7b0a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297981} :answer-field/id #uuid "24506a77-9b74-5997-b750-9ae0f37f53de" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298759} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4004e514-65cc-5ba3-8951-7fdfa32a9481" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4004e514-65cc-5ba3-8951-7fdfa32a9481" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297805} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fb3cc92-18ef-57d1-8cf8-4873a0f63452" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298907} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67ac13fb-5f80-5b63-8caf-0023f6f87094" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297998}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67ac13fb-5f80-5b63-8caf-0023f6f87094" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297998} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1529332-216e-5593-b381-6e2408117b50" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299347}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "34cd5f5a-f82e-5ae5-899e-5e1bd32cf8b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-320021" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\">$ABC=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix, and $C$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $1\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding only $1$ entry, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $2\\times 3$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6\\cdot (-1)+(-2)\\cdot 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6-6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-12\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $(AB)$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)\\,C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-12\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-24 & 48 & -60\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326920 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115227 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8feeacff-b07d-5f98-a765-4d8571674a7a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Associative Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0768e386-ed42-523a-8b81-d32778b33888" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 18 & 9 \\\\ 21 & 7 & -42 \\\\ 8 & 2 & -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324039} {:answer/id #uuid "5765f40b-6dcf-5301-9949-f4819aec1ba2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ 42 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324697} {:answer/id #uuid "8bca11ec-165a-537d-b134-38df44b671e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}21 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 18 & 9 & -42 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325158} {:answer/id #uuid "a36dc3f4-9f65-59e6-9311-6f889cfc4cbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-18 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 42 & 0 & -21 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325358} {:answer/id #uuid "f31eb4fa-cff2-5b17-9422-8db3c6117a17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-144" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326112}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a36dc3f4-9f65-59e6-9311-6f889cfc4cbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-18 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 42 & 0 & -21 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325358} :answer-field/id #uuid "b79923e4-1da4-5e24-8a5e-c420b9db32e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326548}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0594dca0-de16-5429-abef-c4b9b45aec7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-42001" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix, and $C$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding $3$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $2\\times 3$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $AB$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-18 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 42 & 0 & -21 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115836 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115226 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7ad52ce-d408-5390-b91f-c855274f39ea" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Distributive Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13773284-d540-59d5-9332-97c84b837ffe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & 1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{5} & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{7} & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484855} {:answer/id #uuid "a397a770-fb84-5803-b445-bb962f0edcc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{2} & -1 & -\\sqrt{3} \\\\ -1 & -\\sqrt{5} & -1 \\\\ -\\sqrt{7} & -1 & -\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485172} {:answer/id #uuid "bd233e28-d1ff-5b24-a20c-c4ce4f8e0913" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485224} {:answer/id #uuid "ca909ceb-d495-5fda-9394-cd7bfc79f6cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{2} & -2 & -2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ -2 & -2\\sqrt{5} & -2 \\\\ -2\\sqrt{7} & -2 & -2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485248} {:answer/id #uuid "d61c9def-9523-5682-a82f-7beb698de51e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485266}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca909ceb-d495-5fda-9394-cd7bfc79f6cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{2} & -2 & -2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ -2 & -2\\sqrt{5} & -2 \\\\ -2\\sqrt{7} & -2 & -2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485248} :answer-field/id #uuid "5acf797e-8560-5305-87b5-ad22ffde0a24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113953}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "008d2c2b-6bdc-5e16-92ee-368e3b3e4390" :question/math-academy-id "q-42263" :question/problem "Find $AB+CB$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -5 & -1 \\\\ -9 & 10 & 11\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & 1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{5} & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{7} & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 9 & -10 & -13\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nAB+CB=(A+C)B.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $A+C$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+C & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -5 & -1 \\\\ -9 & 10 & 11\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 9 & -10 & -13\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-2{I}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB+CB & =(A+C)B \\\\  & =-2{I}_{3}B \\\\  & =-2B \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{2} & -2 & -2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ -2 & -2\\sqrt{5} & -2 \\\\ -2\\sqrt{7} & -2 & -2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329640 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115228 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Matrix Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98d094e2-1177-5e99-96ad-7caeee897640" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450618} {:answer/id #uuid "ca99c815-da6d-51d7-a07d-611d7659f788" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450619}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98d094e2-1177-5e99-96ad-7caeee897640" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450618} :answer-field/id #uuid "c30fd7ce-bd14-59fb-ab10-845f8a59bb92" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451263} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "956b7a25-6517-5ef2-837c-39c50a5c5a32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450620} {:answer/id #uuid "bd63bdd4-4b06-56ad-b67b-a613cc1dd46f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd63bdd4-4b06-56ad-b67b-a613cc1dd46f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450621} :answer-field/id #uuid "382ec9ba-1720-5328-8c38-f194ab93dcab" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451264} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "762ad639-2afc-55e3-bdc7-be4e7057c714" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450622} {:answer/id #uuid "7a78eef3-ff9c-56b5-98cb-545a4b324d66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450623}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "762ad639-2afc-55e3-bdc7-be4e7057c714" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450622} :answer-field/id #uuid "800a3551-29f1-5bb8-a3bc-66ca201c01c9" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451265}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "005a0156-3d99-59d1-ab99-adf9b9b4c7b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-42264" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $2\\times 2$ matrices, which of the following statements are always true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $AB=BA$\n\n- **II.** $(AB)C=A(BC)$\n\n- **III.** $A(B-C)=(B-C)A$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is true. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $(AB)C=A(BC)$ in general.\n\n- Statement III is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $A(B-C)\\ne (B-C)A$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115837 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115228 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Matrix Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1067aa3d-2b51-5b1a-b638-8cd254e921c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448632} {:answer/id #uuid "a3967aa3-4b50-5c5c-b5fe-aa477f5fe032" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1067aa3d-2b51-5b1a-b638-8cd254e921c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448632} :answer-field/id #uuid "149d811f-1bfd-59da-848a-31d1c4100def" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449356} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86075d40-0e3f-586b-9449-798158d86bca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448634} {:answer/id #uuid "1fec6718-135d-53ed-ace0-3373f23e193b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1fec6718-135d-53ed-ace0-3373f23e193b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448635} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cdc4938-08ac-5768-9c3a-6cf1b96bf157" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449357} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8546691d-f8b4-5754-96f8-903691eb5eb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448636} {:answer/id #uuid "d2f078ae-15b0-55b8-85f1-fb559cdbab88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2f078ae-15b0-55b8-85f1-fb559cdbab88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448637} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bc3e7d1-fdc0-5ebf-9944-36f12a7d8eff" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449358}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5e648555-87e2-52bf-ac70-24ae7f7d32c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-42265" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $4\\times 4$ matrices, which of the following statements are always true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $AB=BA$\n- **II.** $(AB)C=A(BC)$\n- **III.** $AC+BC=(A+B)C$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is true. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $(AB)C=A(BC)$ in general.\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $(A+B)C=AC+BC,$ and $A(B+C)=AB+AC$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statements II and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485543 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115226 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7ad52ce-d408-5390-b91f-c855274f39ea" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Distributive Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6afbb954-8251-54c6-9289-3b7b67977c2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3\\sqrt{2} & 3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 6 & 3\\sqrt{3} & 6 \\\\ 9 & 6 & 3\\sqrt{5}\\text{ }\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485049} {:answer/id #uuid "9f8c7b20-ab9a-5f82-aa71-ab274f566e4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485162} {:answer/id #uuid "a457aec9-c905-57bd-a32b-334aab799f02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485175} {:answer/id #uuid "d93c949b-2601-5a6c-bdfe-2a018e7d7553" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -\\sqrt{2} & -\\sqrt{3} \\\\ -2 & -\\sqrt{3} & -2 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485273} {:answer/id #uuid "dbc1e4f5-2794-5ee2-870f-276a9e8a1fc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{3} & 2 \\\\ 3 & 2 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6afbb954-8251-54c6-9289-3b7b67977c2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3\\sqrt{2} & 3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 6 & 3\\sqrt{3} & 6 \\\\ 9 & 6 & 3\\sqrt{5}\\text{ }\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485049} :answer-field/id #uuid "1201651f-fb8b-5f4f-9fec-edb4aa86cc4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485374}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "72e0b567-7c07-513e-b4b8-2088d6f698dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-75612" :question/problem "Find $AC+BC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -6\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 6 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 9\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{3} & 2 \\\\ 3 & 2 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nAC+BC=(A+B)C.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $A+B$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+B & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -6\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 6 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =3{I}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC+BC & =(A+B)C \\\\  & =3{I}_{3}C \\\\  & =3C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3\\sqrt{2} & 3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 6 & 3\\sqrt{3} & 6 \\\\ 9 & 6 & 3\\sqrt{5}\\text{ }\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345115 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115228 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Matrix Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5b4b6c9-b120-5669-8778-9d44bd03a705" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451627} {:answer/id #uuid "5c9ff174-54f1-5fc0-82c9-56c7f68be83b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451628}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c9ff174-54f1-5fc0-82c9-56c7f68be83b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451628} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6596886-eb35-5a15-8678-0d03898ac57c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452661} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b1b7dcd-0a45-5a31-b1e7-359ba6b8ce48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451629} {:answer/id #uuid "2844641e-66b1-56cc-8371-e36f6a1b3ff0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451630}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b1b7dcd-0a45-5a31-b1e7-359ba6b8ce48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451629} :answer-field/id #uuid "648f05bf-a002-5add-8c9a-e67860f117ba" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452662} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aec13ecc-22bc-5436-b215-dddd0d181f9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451631} {:answer/id #uuid "ddfc103f-6039-5ed8-b224-6f15716dcaa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451632}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aec13ecc-22bc-5436-b215-dddd0d181f9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451631} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ce1dbe9-397b-565f-a4c9-e832cb32d032" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452663}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1c88851c-8567-55d2-897e-8b0f9b020c35" :question/math-academy-id "q-75662" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $7\\times 7$ matrices, which of the following statements are always true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A(B+C)=AC+AB$\n- **II.** $A(BC)=(BA)C$\n- **III.** $AB=BA$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so \n\n$$\nA(B+C)=AB+AC=AC+AB\n$$\n\n since matrix addition is commutative.\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $(AB)C=A(BC)$ in general. However, since matrix multiplication is not commutative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(BC)=(AB)C\\ne (BA)C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485559 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115228 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Matrix Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0baea8e6-67f2-5e1f-8d1f-49751d15a460" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484839} {:answer/id #uuid "150d4133-0a25-50d9-a5b6-3426cedc7ceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484857} {:answer/id #uuid "b6bd451c-1d47-509f-8a91-0bb7d9a2e039" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485211} {:answer/id #uuid "b779c7a3-5d4b-56ea-9ee5-63a3e5e72954" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485212} {:answer/id #uuid "d6de882f-5289-5eb0-83ae-5e40d163532c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485268}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0baea8e6-67f2-5e1f-8d1f-49751d15a460" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484839} :answer-field/id #uuid "72242043-aa0f-565d-a557-78a4b73b318a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485413}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "96d290b8-46cc-5702-9916-bb75bce9f305" :question/math-academy-id "q-75663" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $4\\times 4$ matrices, and ${I}_{4}$ is the $4\\times 4$ identity matrix,  which of the following statements are always true?\n\nI. $A{I}_{4}={I}_{4}A$\n\nII. $(CA)B=C(AB)$\n\nIII. $BC=CB$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is not commutative in general, however, multiplication by the identity matrix is always commutative. In this case, we have  $A{I}_{4}={I}_{4}A=A.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Matrix multiplication is asociative, so $(CA)B=C(AB)$ in general.\n\n- Statement III is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $BC\\ne CB$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statements I  and II are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345117 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115228 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Matrix Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d29adab0-49f5-5be8-9dfb-41b652b9f78b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451639} {:answer/id #uuid "aae53705-b1e7-5ad4-a458-fc12bd5715e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d29adab0-49f5-5be8-9dfb-41b652b9f78b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451639} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ec2f6a3-b7c4-5dbf-b313-e1460364d497" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452667} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "163312b5-47ae-51a4-8302-780627f27eaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451641} {:answer/id #uuid "8391eb9d-de48-5257-958c-71e626ee3926" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451642}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "163312b5-47ae-51a4-8302-780627f27eaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451641} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e9e4ab6-972e-5a28-8a06-204e593f15c3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452668} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5abcda23-f4db-5653-8749-2127e4eb2cc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451643} {:answer/id #uuid "83789ace-8be4-5fa7-bb78-667b324a5f43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451644}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83789ace-8be4-5fa7-bb78-667b324a5f43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451644} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebdef35b-4dc7-5168-954f-85f588629353" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452669}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8ca7b9cd-e052-55a9-b9b9-9f438a40909d" :question/math-academy-id "q-75717" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $6\\times 6$ matrices which of the following statements are always true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $CB=BC$\n- **II.** $A(B-C)=AB-CA$\n- **III.** $A(BC)=(AB)C$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $A(B-C)=AB-AC,$ but $AC\\ne CA$ because matrix multiplication is not commutative in general.\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is associative and  $A(BC)=(AB)C$ is always true.\n\nTherefore, only statement  III is true."}]}
